d="k78" value="1" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];fontSize=11;fontColor=#1A1A1A;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;spacing=1;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="k76"><mxGeometry x="0.566" relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="13.5" y="-0.7" as="offset"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="k79" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read it&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A solid line is an association; the numbers at its ends say how many (1 exactly one, 0..1 zero or one, 0..* zero or more, 1..* one or more). A filled diamond means composition: the part cannot exist without the whole (an application without its casting call). A dashed open arrow means &quot;uses&quot;: a service calls another service or changes that class. Attributes start with -, methods with +; [0..1] marks an optional value. Service methods that take an actor check that person's permission first. ProjectService.addEpisode and publishEpisode are for series, a Should feature; a film's single episode is created and published together with the project. CreditService.add, for someone without an Aflami account, is Should too. Credit.filmRole uses the FilmRole list in diagram 2." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#BBBBBB;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1012.0" width="2264" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>